<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23206" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαίδαλ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cunningly</i> or
				<i>curiously wrought,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάχαιρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					4.59
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Did.
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δαιδάλου</span> codd.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέπλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					635
				</span></i>
			: in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only neut. as Subst., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὃς
				χερσὶν ἐπίστατο δαίδαλα πάντα τεύχειν . . </span> to
			frame all <i>cunning works,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.60
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεκτόνων δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					5.36
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>C.</u>
				1.355
			</span></i>: also in sg., <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				19.227
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>spotted, speckled,</i> or perh. rather, <i>sheeny, shot with
				light,</i> of fish, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>C.</u>
				1.58
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as pr. n.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δαίδαλος, ὁ,</span>
			<i>Daedalus,</i> i. e. <i>the Cunning Worker, the Artist,</i>
			traditional name for the first sculptor, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				18.592
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Men.</u>
				97d
			</span></i>: hence <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαίδαλα, τά,</span>
			=
			<i>statues,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				9.3.2
			</span></i>: also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δαίδαλα, τά,</span> festival of Hera at Argos, ib., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Daed.</u>
			</span></i>tit.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
